speechtext:
That is what the proposition is. If any hon. gentlemen can tell me of any one who would listen to that proposition for a moment, I should like to hear from him. I want to say something to the hon. member for Willow Bunch. I happened to be behind the curtain and I heard him say that he came to the Department of National Revenue himself, and had sent two or three others also to find out what would happen to Roumanian oil or gasoline.
I believe I have had some slight connection with the Department of National Revenue;
I am always glad to see members of parliament, but the hon. member for Willow Bunch never came to see me. Apparently he was not very keen to find out what would happen to the Roumanian oil, but I will tell him what would have happened. If that oil had been sent here upon terms such as one honest man would have used in transacting business with another it would have been permitted to come in under the tariff which this parliament has ordained. That is a simple answer to a simple question. If the hon. member for Willow Bunch or his friends had some oil in Rou-mania and thought the time favourable to dump that oil upon Canada's market to the detriment of the business men of Canada, then the department would have taken care of that situation.
